{
  "about": "Intermediate checkpoints of the WI portrait decoder (spec/wi-codec.md, section 14) for the six public card vectors of public-vectors.json (same index). Every hash is SHA-256 of the byte string that section 14 defines. int32 arrays are little-endian, row-major, over exactly the region named. C4_coefficients is the SHA-256 of an empty string, with count 0, for a level that the skip count leaves uncoded; C5 then equals C3. C8_portrait equals portrait_sha256 in public-vectors.json. Computed from an instrumented copy of the reference codec and reproduced by an independent implementation of the spec.",
  "spec": "spec/wi-codec.md",
  "order": [
    "C1_ll",
    "C2_map",
    "level 4: C3, C4, C5",
    "level 3: C3, C4, C5",
    "level 2: C3, C4, C5",
    "level 1: C3, C4, C5",
    "C6_sharpened",
    "level 0: C3, C4, C5",
    "C7_raster",
    "C8_portrait"
  ],
  "checkpoints": {
    "C1_ll": "LL band after dequantisation: 9 rows x 8 columns, int32",
    "C2_map": "Significance map after the map stage: 250 rows x 200 columns, one byte per cell (1, 2 or 4)",
